<#f0f000>Character-Specific Mechanics</>
Reverse Beat
<#bebebe>Hyde can chain his normal attacks in any given 
order, assuming that the attack hasn't already 
been used in the same chain.

For instance, he can make a chain that goes like this:
_D^C > ^A > ^B > _D^B

However, he CANNOT make a chain that goes like this:
^B > ^A > ^B > ^A</>

<#c92e31>Insulator</>
<#bebebe>All of Hyde's normals that use his sword deal chip damage. 
This chip damage will never KO the opponent, however.</>

<#f0f000>Universal Mechanics</>
Dash				_XFF/~F^A_+^B
Back Dash			_XBB/~B^A_+^B
Super Jump			_TAP_D,_TAP_U
Air Jump			_AIR_U
Air Dash			_AIR_XFF/_XBB
Dead Angle Attack 		_F_+^X while blocking
<#bebebe>(1000 meter required)</>
Rapid Cancel			^X while attacking
<#bebebe>(1000 meter required; 500 for Distortion Drives)</>
Dodge				^Y
Dodge Roll			_B_+^Y/_F_+^Y
Grab				^Z (Air OK)
<#bebebe>Can be used while dashing</>
Burst				^Y_+^Z when hit
Ultra Burst			^Y_+^Z in neutral
Ultra Dead Angle		^Y_+^Z while blocking
<#bebebe>Can only be used if Burst is available</>